  "issue_number": 67,
  "issue_title": "envfile: inline # comments in secrets.env values are not stripped",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n\n`trinity.envfile._parse_env_line()` treats `#` inside a value as literal text. A line like:\n\n```env\nOPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-abc123  # production key\n```\n\nloads `sk-abc123  # production key` into the environment, which breaks API authentication.\n\nFull-line comments (`# comment`) work; inline trailing comments do not.\n\n## Repro\n\n```python\nfrom trinity.envfile import _parse_env_line\nassert _parse_env_line(\"OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-abc123  # production key\") == (\"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\", \"sk-abc123\")\n```\n\nCurrently returns `(\"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\", \"sk-abc123  # production key\")`.\n\n## Expected\n\n- Unquoted values: strip trailing inline comments beginning with ` #` (space + hash), matching common `.env` conventions\n- Quoted values: preserve `#` inside the quotes (`KEY=\"value # kept\"`)\n- Existing full-line comment behavior unchanged\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Inline comment stripping for unquoted values\n- [ ] Quoted values with `#` remain intact\n- [ ] Regression tests in `tests/test_envfile.py`",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-12T23:30:38.000Z",
  "test_cmd": [
    "python",
    "-m",
    "pytest",
    "--tb=short",
    "-q",
    "tests/test_envfile.py"
  ],
